# Opus -- the speech-and-music codec, here for the same reason flac is: it is
# one fifth of libsndfile's all-or-nothing xiph group, and libsndfile is what
# pulseaudio's client library takes as a bare dependency() that no option can
# drop.
#
# BLFS 12.4, pinned here rather than in versions.env: versions.env is
# regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh, so a desktop
# pin placed there is destroyed by the next `make pin`.
SRC_URL=https://downloads.xiph.org/releases/opus/opus-1.5.2.tar.gz
SRC_SHA256=65c1d2f78b9f2fb20082c38cbe47c951ad5839345876e46941612ee87f9a7ce1
SRC_DIR=opus-1.5.2

# BUILT WITH MESON, WHICH IS WHAT BLFS DOES AND NOT WHAT THE TARBALL LEADS WITH.
# opus ships a full autotools tree (configure, Makefile.am, config.guess) and a
# CMakeLists.txt as well. The book's pin beats the tarball's own default, per
# the README's Versions policy, and it is also the cheaper of the three here:
# the autotools path would drag in the config.guess question and the cmake path
# a second build system for one leaf library.
#
# -Dasm=disabled IS THE ONE FLAG WORTH READING TWICE, and it costs nothing.
# meson.build:277 is
#
#     perl = find_program('perl', required: get_option('asm'))
#
# and it sits AFTER the endif of the `host_cpu_family == 'arm' and
# opt_fixed_point` block, not inside it -- so with asm left at its 'auto'
# default, perl is looked up on EVERY architecture whether or not any assembly
# could be used. That is an undeclared find_program (the class
# tools/check-recipes.sh exists to catch) and an artefact that depends on
# whether perl happened to be in the builder image.
#
# Disabling it loses NOTHING here, and that is measured from the source rather
# than assumed: the assembly is guarded by `host_cpu_family == 'arm'` -- meson
# reports aarch64 as 'aarch64', never 'arm' -- AND by opt_fixed_point, which is
# false in this build. Two independent gates, each already closed on both
# architectures this tree targets. What aarch64 actually uses is NEON through
# the intrinsics path below, which -Dasm has nothing to do with.
#
# -Drtcd, -Dasm and -Dintrinsics ARE LEFT AT 'auto' DELIBERATELY -- except asm,
# which is pinned above -- and this is the one place in this tree where auto is
# the right answer rather than a hazard. Finding 4's hazard is an auto feature
# that resolves against WHAT HAPPENS TO BE INSTALLED; these two resolve against
# what the COMPILER AND TARGET CAN DO, through cc.compiles() probes and nothing
# else. There is no find_program and no dependency() anywhere in either path, so
# there is no ambient package that can change the answer. Pinning them
# 'enabled' would instead assert that every future target has the instructions,
# which is the failure mode this comment is avoiding.
#
# -Ddeep-plc, -Ddred, -Dosce: opus 1.5 added neural speech enhancement. All
# three already default 'disabled'; stated because a reader who knows 1.5 added
# them will otherwise go looking for whether this build carries them, and
# because they are the options most likely to be switched on by someone who has
# not costed the model data.
#
# -Ddocs=disabled: the only other find_program in the file
# (meson.build:683, doxygen, required: get_option('docs')). Same argument as
# flac's --disable-doxygen-docs -- today it resolves to nothing, and it would
# start building documentation into a directory finish_install deletes on the
# first rebuild after anyone packages doxygen.
#
# -Dtests and -Dextra-programs disabled: build time for binaries this package
# does not install.
MESON_ARGS="-Dasm=disabled \
-Ddeep-plc=disabled -Ddred=disabled -Dosce=disabled \
-Ddocs=disabled -Dtests=disabled -Dextra-programs=disabled"
